I've been playing way too much 'hack lately (though, is too much ever
enough?). In my marathon I've managed to finally ascend each class,
having gotten really rather good at it now. I've never posted a YAAP
before, but now I feel compelled... this was my most difficult
ascension ever. Anyway, fair warning: I'm long-winded and this YAAP is
a bit of a novella. The only reason I've written it up was that I
think it's a really good one, so, if you like long YAAPs, read on!

---

I'd forgotten how hard an ARC can be... low-damage pick and terrible
armor (if it can even be called that) to start (though digging for
gems and cash is sweet). But I've had so many failed starts trying to
play the ARC again, even without attempting conduct challenges; so,
since I've finally managed to make the ascension a few minutes ago,
with the most unlucky character, here's my YAAP.

Our intrepid adventurer Jones' pet dog Puddles died at the bottom of a
pit within moments of his sad existence, leaving me without a BUC-
checker until I found an altar on level 8. I burned through my food as
it seemed like no-one was home and edible within the dungeon.
Meanwhile, on levels 2 and 3 there were absolutely massive liquor
emporiums! I could barely afford anything, but managed to grab a nice
stack of water to bless once I made it to that altar. Then I found
Snickersnee just lying on the floor somewhere, but the ARC can't train
in it unless a longsword is donated by his deity. Still, I used it
against some large creatures.

Armor was nowhere to be found; no spellbooks to make up for it, and no
useful rings. And no unicorns' horns to be had, not that I could
manage killing one to pry it off its head. Thankfully, I made it to
that altar on level 8 and was able to BUC-check items, but had no
price-checking to help in the ID process. Being so poor in level, HP,
equipment, and still without a decent pet, Jones hit the first couple
levels of Sokoban for some eats before leaving for the mines, knowing
I couldn't tackle the penthouse zoo yet, and deciding I had to get to
a general store already.

Off into the mines... my new pet died almost instantly, and so I
picked up next to no gear from any fallen peace-loving dwarves or
gnomes. I made a bee-line to Minetown, found a general store, and
began checking items, to reveal no scrolls of ID, enchants, remove
curse in either my sack or available for purchase (I had little money
anyway). But... praise be Quetzlpretzel: a cloak of invisibility! The
altar, of course, was presided over by a chaotic priest. No money, no
protection. Finally, I found a new pet (Weirdo the cat), and together
we cleared out the above two levels to finally score a mithril coat
and a mattock. I now felt invincible! I descended into the levels
below, and encountered one of the many previous incarnations of Jones
in ghostly form, along with the lich that had killed him. Lots of
running around. The previous Jones was as poor off as this one, but I
picked up some barely useful, cursed items, so... there was that.

But finally, I got a break and found a wand of polymorph. Oh.
Important note: for the first time ever, I was attempting to go poly-
less, without genocide, without wishing, and without Elbereth.

I picked up a new pet and turned it into a rock troll, which I named
Vice President Dick Cheney, as I do all my troll pets. We returned to
town and the Veep killed off the captains. Did one have a silver
saber? Of course not. We then made it to the bottom level to discover
it was the version filled with undead, including vampires and wraiths.
Lots of running around, and I managed to finally grab the...
lodestone, as I got ported back outside the mines. Without Dick.

Back down to the altar at level 8. Kill, offer, pray, drop the
lodestone, kill, offer, pray, rinse, repeat, congratulations, you've
won Demonbane (and more importantly, the ability to train in
longsword)! Take on Sokoban, survive by gaining pets in the zoo, grab
a BoH, return to the mines, say Hi to my former pet, now quite
hostile, and grab the luckstone. I now had enough money to buy 2 whole
points of protection, and did so. I really should have seen if Dick
would kill off the shopkeepers.

Return to my favorite altar. Gain another artifact... Giantslayer!
Thanks for playing. But by this time I'd trained longsword to basic,
and was working to gain basic in dual-wielding, using Snickersnee and
a pick axe (I'd earlier enchanted it to +2!), occasionally switching
off to the mattock. (Speaking of this dual-wielding combo, question:
would it have been wiser to use two pick axes, with my expert skill?)
I now had incredible armor: a mithril coat, cloak of invisibility,
leather gloves, hard boots, and dwarf helmet... not one of which was
enchanted. I found Cleaver just lying around, and stashed it. I got a
magic lamp, tinning kit, BoH, magic whistle, which were all very
valuable. (I was hoping to tin some nymphs, leppercauns, and tengus to
eventually gain teleportitis and control.) Still no scrolls of ID,
enchant armor, remove curse, but I'd gotten a book of detect monsters,
and was working on my divination skill (using strangely low mana). I
found a new pet and polymorphed it into Mummie Dearest, the giant
mummy. She finally got me my unicorn horn.

Level 12 featured another altar, the last alignable one I'd ever find
(except for that in Minetown). We found the archaeology university and
cleared out the first level of critters, picking up a few items,
notably a book of extra healing (which I could barely cast) and boots
of speed AND WW... finally! I couldn't continue as I was two levels
too weak, and that was fine, since I knew I hadn't a chance of killing
the Minion of Huhetotl, which I think might be the toughest quest
boss.

Level 13: my last store, a huge hardware store, Home Depot! It had
next to nothing I wanted. Mummie Dearest punished the shopkeeper for
his lack of a decent selection; I really had all the tools I'd needed
(why is it that every figurine I find is of an iguana or an acid
blob?!).

Level 14: featured a leprauchan hall, and now I finally returned all
the way back up and down to Minetown, buying several points of
protection with their pots o' gold. It would have been fun for Mummie
Deariest to take out the remaining residents in town, but she got
level-ported along the way, and I never saw her again. Meanwhile, I'd
kind of forgotten about those big liquor emporiums. The general
store's shopkeeper was out of cash, I wasn't strong enough to kill the
priest... a huge collection of potions would have been game-changing!
I needed a new, vicious pet that I could take shopping/murdering.

Level 15: Fort Ludios! I'd have had no chance there. Move along. But
after a few more levels, I finally found an item I'd needed: a ring of
conflict. I had fun storming the castle (well, fort; castle would come
later), survived, exited with the only dragon scales that dropped,
those of a white dragon (of course!, since I already had cold
resistance). It would be a while still before I found my first scroll
of enchant armor, so I stashed it until I finally found a book of
magic missile (the most powerful/useful spell in the game IMHO, after
ID perhaps), at which point I chose the lesser AC to cast spells (I
also downgraded from my +1 dwarf helm to a +0 elven cap). This was
useful once I returned to levels 2 and 3 with my latest pet (I don't
even remember what it was) and picked up literally 60+ potions, some
of which were gain energy. Needless to say, for the rest of the game I
had an ample supply of holy water (to the point where I was blessing
all of my non-bagged items). Since we were all the way up there, I
went down to Minetown yet again (this was getting pretty tedious), and
bought another point of protection before my pet had a priest for
lunch (as well as the shopkeepers, sans Izchak!). More useless spells,
but a robe! Cast extra healing at every opportunity. I offered and
prayed some more, and got another artifact: Sunsword! Meh. Now I was
carrying around a +2 pick axe, +1 Snickersnee, and would switch off to
Demonbane and Sunsword as appropriate.

Down 20 levels to Medusa, the Castle, and Valley of the Dead. All went
well. Finally, a silver saber! And silver dragon scales! And I'd since
found that elusive scroll of enchant armor, though I had none left,
and my one magic marker during the whole game needed recharging. So
now I was wearing unenchanted silver scales, even though I'd since
echanted my white dragon armor to scale mail. Still, I was able to
dump my amulet of reflection for life-saving. Finally: I was ready for
my quest. An invincible level 16! A stunning -15 AC! Almost 200 HP! I
was now intrinsically invisible, wearing a burnt robe, and had
upgraded to some awesome +1 gloves.

Level 12, again: Off I go to confront the Minion of Huhetotl, this
time, bearing a secret weapon: a wand of death! I cut a swath through
my enemies, zap the Minion repeatedly... to discover that the Minion
of Huhetotl is immune to wands of death. Run! Somehow I managed to
ditch him two levels below the university (the REAL life-saver: ring
of teleport control).

Descend to Gehennom. Gain levels (I never succeeded, during the whole
game, in finding a potion of enlightenment to mix with all my
levitation potions). At some point I step onto a polymorph trap and
lose my attempt at poly-selfless conduct, though I'm still good for
not polypiling. When I hit 20th level, I found another saber,
enchanted it all the way to +2, and returned to finish some business
with the university-threatening Minion. I managed it, triumphantly
laughed at my monitor, grabbed my Orb of Detection, and proceeded back
through Gehennom. Along the way I learned charm monster, which saved
me repeatedly. I'd also learned detect treasure and had stockpiled my
obj det potions, so I spent a long time scrounging every level for
anything that could help me, since I needed all the help I could get.

Level 49: I found the very bottom of the dungeon. I searched for the
vibrating square for ages and probably passed over it twice before
catching it. I returned upward to take on Vlad; I'd wanted to do so
sooner, since his tower is a good source of items, but I'd somehow
missed his stairs. I went all the way back up to the Valley of the
Dead and down a dozen levels again before finding it hidden under a
boulder. I killed the underpowered Vlad, and then went on to take out
Rodney with a wand of death.

I'd chugged plently of potions along the way to max abilities, level
(30), and boost my energy a great deal. By the time I entered the
final level, I had +0 silver dragon scale mail, +0 cloak of
displacement, +3 speed boots, +1 dex gauntlets, and a +1 elven cap,
and wielded +5 and +1 sabers. I had the ring collection (free action,
regen, slow digestion, lev, conflict). I'd made an attempt at
teleportitis and control, and got the former but not the latter; I at
least picked up poly control.

I had amazing luck going back up through Gehennom... I think I got
sent back a level only three times! As Rodney sent clusters of
monsters to surround me, I charmed them, at one point having an army
of 13 dragons, trolls, green slimes (!), and more. I got back to my
altar and stash on level 12, retrieved my huge hoard of gems and
artifacts, and then decided to create and sacrifice tons of monsters
to try for another artifact (read: Grayswandir), even though I'd
already had so many that it was kind of a silly idea. But I was also
praying (literally) for an ID or remove curse book (which I of course
never got).

Then I made a hysterical mistake. While I'd stashed most of my pets
one level down (to prevent them from eating all the corpses I'd
created to sacrifice), at one point things got a bit confusing... and
I ended up sacrifcing a dead pet. I'm guessing that that's what lost
me all my points of protection? My AC was now a not-so-invincible -8.
I continued and got back in Quetzpretzel's good graces, but was again
in a pathetic state for AC.

I made my way to the elemental planes, without any pets, as I was set
to go on a major conflict-fest. Though I'd boosted my HP to a
ridiculous extent, I knew that I could only take so many hits. I wish
I could've eaten a ring of regeneration, which I've never done before
for fear of crazy hunger while bearing the AoY and wearing another
amulet and two rings (often not wearing slow digestion, as I never
leave home w/o my free action). Has anyone done this? I'm sure some
have, but I'd like to hear about how rough it was.

The priceless Orb of Detection helped get me where I needed to go,
hitting the portals as quickly as possible. I made it to the astral
plane, accepted an angry angel that was not amused by my conflicting
presence, and charged through to the left-hand section. I played it as
smart as I could, managed to get through to the temple, and was elated
when I found it to be my law-abiding altar. I forgot my semi-clever
plan of taking out my elven dagger and naming it Sting before offering
up the amulet. Meh!


Jones the DWF ARC done ascended.


Level 30, 544 HP, AC -8, maxed abilities.

+5 and +1 silver sabers, +0 silver dragon scale mail, +0 cloak of
displacement, +3 dexterity gauntlets, +3 burnt speed boots, +1 burnt
elven cap
Snickersnee, Demonbane, Giantslayer, Sunsword, Cleaver, Orb of
Detection, Bell of Opening, Book of the Dead, Candelabrum of
Invocation
14 amulets, 187 gems, 0 gold

Most instrinsics, not including teleport control, regeneration; I had
aggravate monster and was the Hand of Elbereth.
Conduct: no genocides, wishes, polymorphing of items (or scrawling of
Elbereth).

3,454 creatures vanquished, 70 of which were really annoying gremlins
that reproduced like bunnies.
Score: 5,259,062, my personal best. Yay me!


I can't believe you read all of this. Don't you have work to do?



